{"title":"French fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/919667861/0/marginalrevolution~French-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1749031863000,"content":"<blockquote><p>De Gaulle was the target of about thirty serious assassination attempts, two of which — in September 1961 and August 1962 — nearly succeeded.  For some anti-Gaullists, the fixation on de Gaulle became so incorporated into their personality that their original reasons for wanting to kill him were eclipsed by the hatred he inspired.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Hating de Gaulle for accepting Algerian independence was one of those motives for at least one of those attempts.</p>\r\n<p>That bit is from Julian Jackson, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Certain-Idea-France-Charles-Gaulle/dp/0141049537/ref=sr_1_2?crid=1OWDE1GNTFSRP&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.QL2ix-8TeE6h4YA_gWABRWDuhnQyVbWAYB0gB86krTI5zj-Jr2pVpOwQy3Ae5MBfy4f19fywVz47uNk8OBIx798JBdKTj3INV7IzZ-6zK2kDESsRslNZWT-Zay2d1pyLbTFeQMkSuW1gPcnQ4HlSknEWeDVT0kDCaXbTDMb12QHN6K06Ix1jNf2VvnnBvZN4gEfdqBffIivymoC5WPlmTZ21jk8JnE3jGdtzYmfNX0o.yeM7X8FXbhHjays61UTXTzP7ZEBcvYrnXQgDWcoekyg&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=julian+jackson+de+gaulle&amp;qid=1748977870&amp;sprefix=julian+jackson%2Caps%2C199&amp;sr=8-2\" target=\"_blank\">A Certain Idea of France: The Life of Charles de Gaulle</a>, a good book.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/06/french-fact-of-the-day.html\">French fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/919667861/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/919667861/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"